00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:57.260
So that's ambition there.

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:01.100
So what I want you to
get is some basic ideas

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:04.850
of appreciation for the
importance of energy

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:06.260
quantization.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:10.490
And say, you see with
this very simple view,

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:14.640
you can actually
understand a lot of things.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:18.350
So let's start with the wave.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:23.030
I said in the last lecture
when you have an interface,

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.880
because the interface thickness
of the characteristic length

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:26.780
is zero.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:29.750
So it's always good to say
what other wave you have

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.030
[? reflecting, ?] other waves.

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:38.390
So let's start with
the general wave.

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:42.930
You all have learned about
waves in one form or another.

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:46.325
What are the most important
characteristics of waves?

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:54.410
What are the basic
characteristics of these waves?

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.510
You have face.

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:17.250
Let's say go even more basic.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:21.480
Amplitude,
wavelength, frequency.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:23.490
So basic characteristics
of waves.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.630
And when we think
about the frequency,

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:33.720
we're thinking
about time domain.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.600
And when we think
about the wavelengths,

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:40.520
we're thinking
about space domain.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:48.560
So if we-- say I have a wave,
simple wave, a sine wave.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:51.810
Here is the period.

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:56.390
And in the case of time
domain, this period is time.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:06:01.160
In the case of space domain,
this is the wavelength.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:04.250
So time period or wavelengths.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:12.260
But we normally do not
like to write time period.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:16.040
We like to talk about frequency.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:22.100
So can anyone tell me what's
the relation between frequency

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:22.880
and time period?

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:28.430
Mathematics, now.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:29.600
It's a Fourier transform.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:34.540
So if you have
purely a function,

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:37.150
if you have Fourier
transform, the universe

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:40.030
is 2 pi over that period.

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:51.800
So we have period and frequency.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:57.830
This is the Fourier pair.

00:06:57.830 --> 00:07:03.050
Of course, frequency is
a 2 pi over the period.

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:05.690
So at least in
time domain, you're

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.580
very comfortable
with the frequency.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:14.420
And in space domain,
we have wavelengths.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:29.580
What's the corresponding
Fourier inverse?

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:35.080
I'm sorry?

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:36.610
Wave number.

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:42.040
That's probably less
familiar, you don't use often.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:57.940
So the wave number, eta
equals 2 pi over lambda

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:00.820
It's a Fourier pair, right?

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:03.970
And of course, when we
talk about frequency,

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:08.520
there is another
frequency we often use.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:11.400
Angular frequency.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:19.200
So omega is an angular
frequency is 2 pi new.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:27.900
And correspondingly, I
have a k equals 2 pi eta,

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.790
or is 2 pi over lambda.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:36.314
OK, this is a free space.

00:08:36.314 --> 00:08:38.855
AUDIENCE: Nu would be 1 over T.

00:08:38.855 --> 00:08:40.504
AUDIENCE: Yeah, nu [INAUDIBLE].

00:08:40.504 --> 00:08:42.289
GANG CHEN: Nu-- you
were, I'm sorry.

00:08:42.289 --> 00:08:44.210
OK, yes, sorry, sorry.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.570
Now all this has a problem.

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:51.110
1 over T, and otherwise,
we might have 2 pi, there.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:51.710
Thank you.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:58.090
But the space is more
complex than time.

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:04.110
Space has direction.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:09.380
So when a wave traveling in a
certain direction, I can say,

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:12.830
this is the wavelength in
that specific direction.

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:15.650
I can have kx, ky, kz.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:23.370
So here, K, in general,
is a wave vector.

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:25.010
So it's a kx, ky, kz.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:34.220
So we have wave vector.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:36.455
I want to be consistently
using capital.

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:49.145
So this K is the magnitude
of the wave vector.

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:56.950
So now we have the
space, we have the time,

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:59.830
basic characteristics
that characterize

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:02.650
a wave, its periodicity.

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:06.520
And now we can write
this simplest wave,

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:09.400
simple form of a wave.

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:11.860
The simplest way is a
sine wave or cosine wave,

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:14.140
constant amplitude.

00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:16.840
So let's write it a simple wave.

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:21.100
And I'll write using
general symbol, phi.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:23.830
And this could be a vector.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:26.020
It could be a vector wave.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:29.830
Think about, acoustic
wave is the vector wave.

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:34.380
The electromagnetic
wave is a vector wave.

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:40.620
So a vector that
has an amplitude,

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:44.700
and I write a
constant amplitude.

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:51.630
And I have a time, omega
t, minus k, times x.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:55.815
You can go to say, substitute
omega equal 2 pi nu, k

00:10:55.815 --> 00:10:57.660
is 2 pi over lambda.

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:02.890
So this is a wave traveling
in the x direction.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:12.120
And then I have a unit
vector represent this vector.

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:15.910
When I say the direction, that's
the wave traveling direction.

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:17.770
So I have two directions there.

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:20.970
One is the wave
traveling direction.

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:26.620
The other is the wave
oscillation direction.

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:29.430
If you think about the
electromagnetic field,

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:32.410
the wave is traveling forward.

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:36.090
And we know electromagnetic
field is the transverse wave,

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:38.820
so electric field is
perpendicular to the wave

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:40.780
traveling direction.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:44.250
If you think about the
acoustic wave, the sound wave,

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:45.990
it's a longitudinal wave.

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:48.300
So the wave vector
is propagating

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:52.830
to you and the oscillation,
the pressure wave

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:55.360
is also in the same direction.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:57.180
Longitudinal wave.

00:11:57.180 --> 00:11:59.050
So I have two directions.

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:05.490
And this I associate a
polarization of the wave.

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:18.230
And this x is the direction,
the wave propagation direction.

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:24.080
And this is the field, y
is the field direction.

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:27.710
So this is the simple
wave, of course,

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:30.860
a, here is the amplitude.

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:33.410
And somebody
mentioned the phase.

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:37.650
So phase of the wave
is what's inside.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:42.920
So omega t minus kx,
that's the phase.

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:53.420
And for a constant phase, so a
plan of a certain phase value,

00:12:53.420 --> 00:12:57.710
and if this is a constant,
that's a constant phase plan.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:59.980
And you can see
this plan is moving

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:07.450
at dx dt equals omega
over k, from here.

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:10.140
Take a derivative.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:16.340
So that's the velocity
of the constant phase.

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:18.820
So this is called
the phase velocity.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:34.210
And of course, the
most common relation,

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:36.760
you probably familiar,
is the light.

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:41.350
Where you have for
light in vacuum,

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:44.590
we know frequency
times wavelengths

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:46.100
is the speed of light.

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:50.320
I use a small c, or here,
let's put a constant.

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:55.600
And so speed of light, and
this we say, omega equals ck.

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:05.200
For light, it's a linear
relation between omega and k

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:07.390
in free space.

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:11.830
But more generally, as
you will see very soon,

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:16.540
there is a very complex
relation between omega and k,

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:17.890
in general.

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:22.330
So omega and k, in
general case, could

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:27.760
be a very complicated
function of the wave vector.

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:32.530
And what that means is
in different direction,

00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:39.970
the wavelengths and frequency
have very complex relationships

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:44.950
And this is particularly true
when we go to solids, photons,

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:46.430
and electrons.

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:51.070
So that's just a warning
down this street.

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:57.670
And so here we talk about phase,
we talk about sine wave here.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:15:02.110
But in mathematical operation,
if you take a derivative

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:04.630
of sine, what do you get?

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.670
Cosine, right?

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:12.370
And that's not convenient, even
though it's a simple enough.

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:15.100
A simpler derivative
where it goes to itself

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:18.040
is the exponential function.

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:22.690
So very often rather
than representing a wave

00:15:22.690 --> 00:15:26.860
in sine and cosine, I'm
going to represent it

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:29.450
in exponential functions.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:32.110
So this is a complex
representation.

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:45.080
That's really for
mathematical convenience.

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:50.120
And if I use a complex
representation,

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:56.210
I will write this wave as--

00:15:56.210 --> 00:16:01.010
I can combine a and y
into a vector, that's

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:04.890
the wave oscillation direction.

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:12.620
And then I will write
exponential minus i, omega t.

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:19.010
So I use a complex,
omega t minus k times x.

00:16:19.010 --> 00:16:20.150
First I do 1D.

00:16:24.990 --> 00:16:28.290
So if you say this,
of course, it's

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:32.500
easier to take a derivative
of exponential function.

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:38.370
And what I have
here really means I

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:41.310
can write this exponential
back into cosine and sine.

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:49.770
So I have cosine, omega
t minus k, x minus i,

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:53.910
sine omega t minus k, x.

00:16:57.110 --> 00:17:02.790
So I have a real part
and an imaginary part.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:08.040
And in real life, of
course, the waves normally

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:11.250
is either sine and cosine.

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:16.599
So the [? case, ?]
you stick to say, OK,

00:17:16.599 --> 00:17:19.650
if my solution-- if my
initial condition, my boundary

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:25.349
condition, all is for the real
part, cosine, then at the end

00:17:25.349 --> 00:17:28.710
after I solve my problem in
this complex representation,

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:33.090
my real power solution
is what I'm looking for.

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:35.130
If you stick to
the imaginary part,

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:37.830
again, you have to look at
your initial, your boundary

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:39.150
condition.

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:44.850
And as long as you meet
the sign, those constraint,

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:48.490
you say the imaginary
part is your solution.

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:52.440
So that's this
complex representation

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:56.250
gives you mathematical
convenience.

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:58.830
A lot of commonalities,
if you look there,

00:17:58.830 --> 00:18:02.140
I put a minus sign in the front.

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:05.010
That's just my preference.

00:18:05.010 --> 00:18:08.160
It turns out that
even different book,

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:11.940
people sometimes use
positive, some use negative.

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:15.300
And particularly, when
you go to read optics,

00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:18.240
some books use a positive,
some people use negative.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:20.130
And that creates
a lot of confusion

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:23.940
because that will
mean later on, you

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:26.070
will see there is
an after constant

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:28.230
that has a real part
and imaginary part.

00:18:28.230 --> 00:18:31.620
And in the front, it could
be positive or negative sign.

00:18:31.620 --> 00:18:33.870
So unfortunately,
that's the case.

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:40.860
And we don't have
a solution there.

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:43.950
And the other comment
I want to say,

00:18:43.950 --> 00:18:47.940
this waves are traveling waves.

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:50.220
Last lecture, I mentioned
is standing wave.

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:53.490
If you play guitar,
you clamp the two ends.

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:55.035
That's a standing wave.

00:18:55.035 --> 00:18:58.140
And here is a wave
that traveling,

00:18:58.140 --> 00:19:03.660
in this case, omega t minus kx
into the positive x direction.

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:06.390
If it's a plus kx,
that's the wave

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:12.780
traveling into the negative
direction, x direction.

00:19:12.780 --> 00:19:19.030
More generalization, here is
a wave in the x direction.

00:19:19.030 --> 00:19:23.000
But I said k is
generally a vector.

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:26.140
So if I write a
three dimensional,

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:32.260
plane wave and the
general form for this wave

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:35.890
is a, that's again, the
polarization direction.

00:19:35.890 --> 00:19:44.620
And amplitude exponential
minus i, omega t minus k

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:48.310
is a vector dot r.

00:19:48.310 --> 00:19:57.055
So this is a plane wave in
complex representation in 3D.

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:03.830
General space.

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:09.530
And we mentioned here
is a traveling wave.

00:20:09.530 --> 00:20:18.080
And I can use traveling wave to
construct the standing waves.

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:21.170
Example, let's think
about standing wave.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:37.530
So I have two opposing
traveling waves.

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:43.120
Same amplitude, one is
sine omega t minus kx.

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:49.030
So this is a wave traveling
to the positive x direction.

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:56.070
I have opposing wave traveling
in the negative direction, sin

00:20:56.070 --> 00:20:56.805
plus kx.

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:03.620
So two traveling waves, now.

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:07.742
And I superimpose them
together, what do I get?

00:21:10.820 --> 00:21:11.750
Add two sine.

00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:20.110
It's two sines, sine, cosine.

00:21:20.110 --> 00:21:22.150
So the negative part cancel.

00:21:22.150 --> 00:21:29.330
So I will get 2A sin
omega t, cosine kx.

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:39.155
So now you can see I have--

00:21:42.470 --> 00:21:46.380
standing wave because
these are my [INAUDIBLE]..

00:21:46.380 --> 00:21:51.070
When the kx equal 0, it
doesn't depend on time.

00:21:51.070 --> 00:21:54.200
So my zero point is fixed.

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:57.240
You play your guitar,
you press your finger,

00:21:57.240 --> 00:22:01.920
and you fix your loads there.

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:05.610
So this day, I can
use the standing wave

00:22:05.610 --> 00:22:08.430
to construct--
the traveling wave

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:11.700
to construct standing wave.

00:22:11.700 --> 00:22:15.400
Last comment on wave.

00:22:15.400 --> 00:22:18.001
What's the energy of
the wave, typically?

00:22:21.200 --> 00:22:27.050
So energy of wave is typically
proportional to the square.

00:22:27.050 --> 00:22:34.400
So the energy is typically
proportional to the square

00:22:34.400 --> 00:22:35.210
of the wave.

00:22:39.100 --> 00:22:42.710
The amplitude higher,
larger energy.

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:44.808
Those are the basic
characteristics.

00:22:49.100 --> 00:22:54.590
So with this, let's go to
talk about material wave.

00:22:54.590 --> 00:22:58.400
And we have to go into
the quantum mechanics.

00:23:08.420 --> 00:23:10.220
Let's talk about how it started.

00:23:21.840 --> 00:23:27.950
So this is a very interesting
history in science.

00:23:27.950 --> 00:23:33.920
This is the study
about with the optics.

00:23:33.920 --> 00:23:39.200
And you heard probably
Newton optics.

00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:43.790
And of course, when
Newton did the optics,

00:23:43.790 --> 00:23:47.800
he treated light as particles.

00:23:47.800 --> 00:23:51.040
He didn't think
light was a wave.

00:23:51.040 --> 00:23:55.780
And so it took a lot of
time to challenge Newton.

00:23:55.780 --> 00:23:59.710
And there are [INAUDIBLE],, there
are a lot of people eventually

00:23:59.710 --> 00:24:04.480
it was established light is
a wave, its not a particle.

00:24:07.150 --> 00:24:13.390
The final triumph is
Maxwell equations for light.

00:24:13.390 --> 00:24:16.900
So going from particle to wave.

00:24:16.900 --> 00:24:24.900
And Maxwell equations solidify
the wave nature of light.

00:24:24.900 --> 00:24:28.730
And that seems to be
all settled problem.

00:24:28.730 --> 00:24:32.150
Except they say if you go to
look at the history of physics

00:24:32.150 --> 00:24:38.120
and there are two problems
that people wrestle with.

00:24:38.120 --> 00:24:41.420
One is black body radiation.

00:24:51.790 --> 00:24:55.600
And it was found
through experiment

00:24:55.600 --> 00:24:58.580
that this is the wavelength.

00:24:58.580 --> 00:25:01.240
And this is the
emission from black body

00:25:01.240 --> 00:25:04.340
at different wavelengths.

00:25:04.340 --> 00:25:09.610
And this is a typical curve
of blackbody radiation.

00:25:09.610 --> 00:25:17.380
And the classical mechanics
are for black body for light,

00:25:17.380 --> 00:25:21.610
unfortunately, the trend
should be always like this.

00:25:24.250 --> 00:25:30.150
So that was a big puzzle
for physicists at the time.

00:25:30.150 --> 00:25:36.360
And the other is all relate
to photon is the hydrogen

00:25:36.360 --> 00:25:41.425
absorption spectrum.

00:25:49.450 --> 00:25:52.470
And it was observed
that absorption

00:25:52.470 --> 00:25:55.730
happens at discrete lines.

00:25:55.730 --> 00:25:57.940
And the continuing
mechanics say you

00:25:57.940 --> 00:25:59.890
should have a
continuous spectrum,

00:25:59.890 --> 00:26:01.840
but they say the
measurement actually

00:26:01.840 --> 00:26:05.430
say that's not the case.

00:26:05.430 --> 00:26:10.730
So to answer this puzzle,
a lot of people tried,

00:26:10.730 --> 00:26:16.940
and it was Planck that first
introduced a radical concept.

00:26:23.300 --> 00:26:29.870
And rather than-- when we talk
about electromagnetic wave,

00:26:29.870 --> 00:26:32.930
we say the energy is
proportional to empty

00:26:32.930 --> 00:26:35.520
the square.

00:26:35.520 --> 00:26:36.360
It's a continuum.

00:26:36.360 --> 00:26:38.910
You can have any amplitude.

00:26:38.910 --> 00:26:44.910
So what Planck introduced
is that you cannot have any

00:26:44.910 --> 00:26:48.880
continuous function of
that, say amplitude.

00:26:48.880 --> 00:26:51.840
So your energy is not
a continuous function

00:26:51.840 --> 00:26:59.070
and energy at specific
frequency can only be multiple

00:26:59.070 --> 00:27:03.320
of this h nu.

00:27:03.320 --> 00:27:09.320
And this h is the Planck
constant, is 6.6 10

00:27:09.320 --> 00:27:12.755
to the minus 34 joule second.

00:27:16.940 --> 00:27:20.360
n is an integer.

00:27:20.360 --> 00:27:24.050
n is 0, 1, 2.

00:27:24.050 --> 00:27:30.620
So the energy of the
light cannot be any value.

00:27:30.620 --> 00:27:34.860
It has to be multiple
of this h nu.

00:27:34.860 --> 00:27:39.440
So that was a radical concept,
discretization of energy.

00:27:39.440 --> 00:27:43.320
And so what happened was
Einstein, as you know,

00:27:43.320 --> 00:27:51.530
he was a patent clerk, he read
Planck's theory, blackbody.

00:27:51.530 --> 00:27:58.120
And he did another
radical proposal.

00:27:58.120 --> 00:28:06.160
And he say this means that
the electromagnetic wave is

00:28:06.160 --> 00:28:08.730
granular.

00:28:08.730 --> 00:28:12.500
It has particle characteristics.

00:28:12.500 --> 00:28:14.920
So it came back to a particle.

00:28:14.920 --> 00:28:18.790
Particle has energy
and the momentum.

00:28:18.790 --> 00:28:21.010
So what's the momentum of light?

00:28:24.260 --> 00:28:30.995
So Einstein has his famous
energy relation, mc squared.

00:28:35.190 --> 00:28:42.550
And momentum p, is a mass
because the light is not

00:28:42.550 --> 00:28:46.110
a particle that has mass.

00:28:46.110 --> 00:28:48.840
So we need to get
rid of the mass.

00:28:48.840 --> 00:28:57.600
And so is the mc, so we
have mc is mc squared divide

00:28:57.600 --> 00:28:59.650
by c, that's the energy.

00:28:59.650 --> 00:29:02.820
Energy is the h nu divided by c.

00:29:02.820 --> 00:29:05.040
So it's h over lambda.

00:29:08.050 --> 00:29:13.720
So Einstein argue that the
momentum of this light quanta

00:29:13.720 --> 00:29:16.910
is actual lambda.

00:29:16.910 --> 00:29:23.990
And now, the light has
both, say this basic quanta

00:29:23.990 --> 00:29:28.010
has both an energy unit,
h nu and a momentum

00:29:28.010 --> 00:29:29.840
unit of h over lambda.

00:29:32.920 --> 00:29:38.410
So with that, he argued that
light, say, has a particle.

00:29:38.410 --> 00:29:41.395
This is granular wave, it has
both a wave and a particle.

00:29:44.070 --> 00:29:49.605
And in fact, if you go to
read Einstein paper in 1905--

00:29:49.605 --> 00:29:52.800
he published four papers.

00:29:52.800 --> 00:29:58.660
And one is relativity.

00:29:58.660 --> 00:30:03.250
The other was on
Brownian motion.

00:30:03.250 --> 00:30:05.125
Brownian motion
was his PhD thesis.

00:30:07.750 --> 00:30:10.120
At the time, they didn't
know Brownian motion.

00:30:10.120 --> 00:30:12.740
They didn't there was
a Browning observation.

00:30:12.740 --> 00:30:19.770
He was just trying to infer
the size of atoms, molecules.

00:30:19.770 --> 00:30:27.080
And then he hypothesis
this energy quanta.

00:30:27.080 --> 00:30:34.790
And I wasn't sure the
other one was about this

00:30:34.790 --> 00:30:36.260
is the photoelectric effect.

00:30:36.260 --> 00:30:41.380
But I thought this one together
with the photoelectric effect.

00:30:41.380 --> 00:30:43.200
Anybody remember?

00:30:43.200 --> 00:30:45.180
Four papers.

00:30:45.180 --> 00:30:48.420
So if the photoelectric effect
with this together is one

00:30:48.420 --> 00:30:50.250
then I can only count three.

00:30:53.020 --> 00:30:55.090
Maybe you go you
go back to check.

00:30:58.600 --> 00:31:01.130
With this an energy
quanta concept,

00:31:01.130 --> 00:31:05.860
he explained another
experimental observation.

00:31:05.860 --> 00:31:09.010
That's the photoelectric effect.

00:31:09.010 --> 00:31:13.450
And the photoelectric
effect is when you have

00:31:13.450 --> 00:31:16.480
two electrode, metal electrode.

00:31:16.480 --> 00:31:18.700
You shine light onto it.

00:31:18.700 --> 00:31:22.420
You will have a current flow.

00:31:22.420 --> 00:31:23.200
Current flow.

00:31:26.790 --> 00:31:33.840
And the physics is that the
light drive electron out

00:31:33.840 --> 00:31:34.930
of the metal.

00:31:34.930 --> 00:31:39.790
So go from one electrode
to the other electrode.

00:31:39.790 --> 00:31:43.890
But the puzzle was
that you should be--

00:31:43.890 --> 00:31:45.690
the current should
be proportional

00:31:45.690 --> 00:31:48.120
to the intensity of light.

00:31:48.120 --> 00:31:52.430
So the more light that comes,
the higher current you have.

00:31:52.430 --> 00:31:53.810
But the experimental
observations

00:31:53.810 --> 00:31:58.940
is if the light wavelengths,
or say frequency,

00:31:58.940 --> 00:32:01.880
wavelengths are too long,
or frequencies are too low,

00:32:01.880 --> 00:32:03.210
it doesn't have current.

00:32:03.210 --> 00:32:08.400
So there's a threshold for
this photoelectric effect.

00:32:08.400 --> 00:32:14.580
And Einstein's explanation is
this is where electron sits.

00:32:14.580 --> 00:32:18.070
Later on, we'll see
this is the Fermi level.

00:32:18.070 --> 00:32:20.280
And here is the--
it needs to come out

00:32:20.280 --> 00:32:23.520
of the metal to the vacuum.

00:32:23.520 --> 00:32:30.630
And there you got a
difference in energy.

00:32:30.630 --> 00:32:37.485
And this difference here is
vacuum, is the work function.

00:32:46.360 --> 00:32:51.145
That's why you say
you have to have--

00:32:51.145 --> 00:32:54.100
you to have this
energy quanta, h nu,

00:32:54.100 --> 00:32:57.100
larger than the work function.

00:32:57.100 --> 00:32:59.410
And it's like you
get a one ball,

00:32:59.410 --> 00:33:02.230
you knock out another ball.

00:33:02.230 --> 00:33:05.230
So this is the granular,
the consequence

00:33:05.230 --> 00:33:07.870
of this granular
picture of light.

00:33:10.660 --> 00:33:15.550
In fact, if you go to
check the Einstein papers,

00:33:15.550 --> 00:33:19.540
so sometimes I joke,
he's a heat transfer guy.

00:33:19.540 --> 00:33:24.370
If you go to check
Einstein papers, he really,

00:33:24.370 --> 00:33:30.380
all those arguments were
based on thermodynamics.

00:33:30.380 --> 00:33:33.800
If you think about the time,
there was no quantum mechanics.

00:33:33.800 --> 00:33:38.180
And they only had the classical
mechanics and the Boltzmann,

00:33:38.180 --> 00:33:41.930
at the best, the Boltzmann
[INAUDIBLE] for physics.

00:33:41.930 --> 00:33:47.770
That was the foundation at the
time, and Maxwell equations.

00:33:47.770 --> 00:33:53.620
So very interesting to
read those articles.

00:33:53.620 --> 00:33:57.820
And it took, actually,
on this quanta of light,

00:33:57.820 --> 00:34:02.290
it took Einstein another 10
years or so, to think more.

00:34:02.290 --> 00:34:08.960
And came up with the idea
of a stimulated emission.

00:34:08.960 --> 00:34:14.373
That's also further, say,
the light characteristics.

00:34:17.010 --> 00:34:21.570
So with that, we
have basic relation,

00:34:21.570 --> 00:34:23.280
Planck-Einstein relation.

00:34:23.280 --> 00:34:28.199
The energy of the
quanta is h nu,

00:34:28.199 --> 00:34:33.480
and the momentum of the
quanta is h over lambda.

00:34:33.480 --> 00:34:38.070
And this is for EM wave.

00:34:38.070 --> 00:34:42.040
And later on, at the time, they
didn't give the name photon.

00:34:42.040 --> 00:34:45.810
So it wasn't until
1930's, somebody

00:34:45.810 --> 00:34:48.864
suggested that this basic
energy quanta for light

00:34:48.864 --> 00:34:49.739
is called the photon.

00:34:53.420 --> 00:34:59.120
And so that's where Einstein
stopped on this photon.

00:34:59.120 --> 00:35:03.110
And like I said, he said
stimulating emission, all that.

00:35:03.110 --> 00:35:07.750
And then there was
a graduate student,

00:35:07.750 --> 00:35:12.970
his name was de Broglie,
doing his PhD thesis.

00:35:12.970 --> 00:35:17.500
And he looked at this
Planck-Einstein relation

00:35:17.500 --> 00:35:18.640
for the quantum.

00:35:18.640 --> 00:35:24.560
And there is going
from wave to particle.

00:35:24.560 --> 00:35:31.160
And he made a very
bold, extrapolation.

00:35:31.160 --> 00:35:34.670
He said why just for the
electromagnetic wave?

00:35:34.670 --> 00:35:40.340
Why is not for any particle
that also has the reverse wave

00:35:40.340 --> 00:35:42.710
characteristics?

00:35:42.710 --> 00:35:59.095
So de Broglie further
extended this to matter waves.

00:36:07.720 --> 00:36:09.670
He didn't have an equation.

00:36:09.670 --> 00:36:12.690
He couldn't write a,
say, wave equation.

00:36:12.690 --> 00:36:17.860
But I say, I have to admit, I
didn't go to read his thesis.

00:36:17.860 --> 00:36:21.600
But I heard the
thesis was very short.

00:36:21.600 --> 00:36:26.040
And it just says reverse
and make the argument.

00:36:26.040 --> 00:36:30.080
And then people went
to do experiment.

00:36:30.080 --> 00:36:41.180
And they experiment on that
was by Davisson and Germer.

00:36:46.490 --> 00:36:50.330
So if we think about
the material wave,

00:36:50.330 --> 00:36:55.730
let's take the wavelength
of matter is h over p.

00:36:58.640 --> 00:37:02.240
And I can go to calculate
what's the wavelength?

00:37:02.240 --> 00:37:04.970
And I take any
object to 1 kilogram.

00:37:08.070 --> 00:37:13.020
And 1 meter per second,
what's the wavelength?

00:37:13.020 --> 00:37:14.310
That's just the h, right?

00:37:14.310 --> 00:37:17.670
p is mv, is 1.

00:37:17.670 --> 00:37:20.910
And wavelength is
10 to the minus 34.

00:37:20.910 --> 00:37:23.770
So I think this is probably
related to gravitational wave,

00:37:23.770 --> 00:37:25.270
people are still
trying to establish

00:37:25.270 --> 00:37:27.720
the relation between
gravitational waves

00:37:27.720 --> 00:37:30.410
and the quantum
mechanics, all this.

00:37:30.410 --> 00:37:33.120
But that's too short.

00:37:33.120 --> 00:37:36.516
So your m is too large.

00:37:36.516 --> 00:37:40.890
And but see, if you go
to take an electron,

00:37:40.890 --> 00:37:43.590
the electron mass is
10 to the minus 31--

00:37:43.590 --> 00:37:46.750
9.1-- 10 to the minus 31.

00:37:46.750 --> 00:37:49.800
If electron was 1
meter per second,

00:37:49.800 --> 00:37:52.410
the wavelength is very long
because 10 to minus 34,

00:37:52.410 --> 00:37:59.370
divide 10 to minus 31, give
you 10 to the minus 3 meter.

00:37:59.370 --> 00:38:02.190
That's a very long wavelength.

00:38:02.190 --> 00:38:04.660
In fact, it's too long.

00:38:04.660 --> 00:38:09.370
So the Davisson and
Germer experiment

00:38:09.370 --> 00:38:11.650
was actually shooting
electrons-- yes?

00:38:11.650 --> 00:38:15.070
AUDIENCE: Your velocity
is always relative?

00:38:15.070 --> 00:38:18.490
GANG CHEN: Well, let's
say you should go to--

00:38:18.490 --> 00:38:20.710
ideally, you should go
to relativistic velocity,

00:38:20.710 --> 00:38:23.440
so when you go,
actually electron.

00:38:23.440 --> 00:38:25.270
When you say relative
what do you mean?

00:38:25.270 --> 00:38:26.859
Relative to each
other, or relative--

00:38:26.859 --> 00:38:29.276
AUDIENCE: The first example
when you said 1 kilogram and 1

00:38:29.276 --> 00:38:30.280
meter per second--

00:38:30.280 --> 00:38:30.988
GANG CHEN: Right.

00:38:30.988 --> 00:38:35.423
AUDIENCE: And 1 meter per
second is [INAUDIBLE]----

00:38:35.423 --> 00:38:37.840
GANG CHEN: Relative to which
observation system, what they

00:38:37.840 --> 00:38:38.630
mean?

00:38:38.630 --> 00:38:40.240
I don't know.

00:38:40.240 --> 00:38:42.790
Good question.

00:38:42.790 --> 00:38:43.960
OK.

00:38:43.960 --> 00:38:44.740
So--

00:38:44.740 --> 00:38:47.260
AUDIENCE: Relative
to the emitter

00:38:47.260 --> 00:38:50.123
of the electron [INAUDIBLE].

00:38:50.123 --> 00:38:51.540
GANG CHEN: Relative
to the emitter

00:38:51.540 --> 00:38:53.790
of the electron, relative to--

00:38:53.790 --> 00:38:56.790
the question is relative
to what was the observer.

00:38:56.790 --> 00:38:58.895
I think it has to be
relative to the observer.

00:38:58.895 --> 00:39:01.310
AUDIENCE: So the wavelength
is always depending

00:39:01.310 --> 00:39:03.120
on where you are observed.

00:39:03.120 --> 00:39:05.370
GANG CHEN: Yeah, should
be, right we say--

00:39:05.370 --> 00:39:10.110
if you think about Doppler
effect, a moving object emit

00:39:10.110 --> 00:39:12.660
and you have
different wavelengths,

00:39:12.660 --> 00:39:14.800
depending on the speed.

00:39:14.800 --> 00:39:15.300
OK.

00:39:15.300 --> 00:39:19.650
So lambda equals, say, h over p.

00:39:19.650 --> 00:39:23.910
And what they did is shoot
the electron on aluminum foil.

00:39:23.910 --> 00:39:26.475
So aluminum foil has atoms.

00:39:32.080 --> 00:39:36.020
And when you-- it's periodical
arrangement of atoms.

00:39:36.020 --> 00:39:41.320
So when you have a wave
come in and the waves

00:39:41.320 --> 00:39:44.410
see a periodic structure, you
have constructive, destructive

00:39:44.410 --> 00:39:45.560
interference.

00:39:45.560 --> 00:39:46.640
You have diffraction.

00:39:46.640 --> 00:39:50.590
So they only go to
certain directions.

00:39:50.590 --> 00:39:53.550
So what they observe
is they transmit it,

00:39:53.550 --> 00:39:56.790
if you look at the
different directions,

00:39:56.790 --> 00:39:59.820
transmitted electron
has spikes at the angle.

00:40:02.530 --> 00:40:05.530
And that established
the evidence,

00:40:05.530 --> 00:40:10.600
the electrons of waves.

00:40:10.600 --> 00:40:14.720
So all those people got
Nobel prize, of course.

00:40:14.720 --> 00:40:20.530
And so this in fact is the
foundation for the tools

00:40:20.530 --> 00:40:21.700
you'll be using.

00:40:21.700 --> 00:40:24.910
Some of you use in research.

00:40:24.910 --> 00:40:28.615
The typical Transmission
Electron Microscope, TEM.

00:40:43.190 --> 00:40:47.570
Microscope, right?

00:40:47.570 --> 00:40:48.440
So how it works?

00:40:52.550 --> 00:40:57.320
One way is you use a very
sharp tip, [INAUDIBLE] tip.

00:40:57.320 --> 00:41:01.850
You have to apply a
voltage between this tip,

00:41:01.850 --> 00:41:04.100
a high voltage.

00:41:04.100 --> 00:41:05.570
You drive the electron out.

00:41:08.420 --> 00:41:13.280
So this is a field mission, when
your voltage apply high enough

00:41:13.280 --> 00:41:18.500
on tip, the electron get enough
energy to go overcome the--

00:41:18.500 --> 00:41:20.760
jump to the vacuum.

00:41:20.760 --> 00:41:22.650
OK This is a field emission.

00:41:22.650 --> 00:41:25.410
You can also heat this tip.

00:41:25.410 --> 00:41:27.270
That's a thermal emission.

00:41:27.270 --> 00:41:29.760
Get the electron out of the tip.

00:41:29.760 --> 00:41:32.460
And then you apply
another high voltage

00:41:32.460 --> 00:41:35.790
to [INAUDIBLE] this electron.

00:41:35.790 --> 00:41:40.280
And typically,
you say TEM people

00:41:40.280 --> 00:41:42.450
will say how good is a TEM?

00:41:42.450 --> 00:41:46.590
It typically means how short
is the electron wavelengths?

00:41:46.590 --> 00:41:48.600
So you actually want
to [INAUDIBLE] electron

00:41:48.600 --> 00:41:53.100
to very high velocity,
and typically TEM voltage

00:41:53.100 --> 00:42:02.280
is about 100 keV,
100 keV, kilovolt.

00:42:02.280 --> 00:42:05.310
So that's the voltage
applied to the electrons.

00:42:07.890 --> 00:42:11.850
And then say you got the
