00:52:35.480 --> 00:52:50.500
So we have expecting value
and out of any quantity,

00:52:50.500 --> 00:52:51.610
this could be--

00:52:51.610 --> 00:52:56.470
so we use this one is
now a number, expecting

00:52:56.470 --> 00:53:02.560
value of any quantity
is integrated over,

00:53:02.560 --> 00:53:05.740
again, the same volume.

00:53:05.740 --> 00:53:11.630
And the wave function,
for that quantity,

00:53:11.630 --> 00:53:16.670
normal representation
is an operator.

00:53:16.670 --> 00:53:20.630
So this quantity in quantum
mechanics is an operator.

00:53:24.890 --> 00:53:28.310
So we have the
operator operates,

00:53:28.310 --> 00:53:32.960
say, the complex conjugate,
and wave function operate--

00:53:32.960 --> 00:53:36.200
operator operate on the
wave function and times

00:53:36.200 --> 00:53:37.650
the complex conjugate.

00:53:37.650 --> 00:53:42.980
So operator operates on
the function following it.

00:53:42.980 --> 00:53:45.030
What does that mean?

00:53:45.030 --> 00:53:51.980
So let's ride the operator
for a few common quantities.

00:53:51.980 --> 00:54:01.325
For position it's easy,
that's just a normal r.

00:54:05.790 --> 00:54:16.940
But for momentum, this
operator now is a derivative.

00:54:16.940 --> 00:54:24.455
Say a momentum operator
is minus i h bar gradient.

