for the Schrodinger equation.

00:56:57.280 --> 00:57:03.220
I want to get the time
dependent term out first.

00:57:03.220 --> 00:57:08.920
So for that, I assume
the potential energy

00:57:08.920 --> 00:57:13.210
as a function of space only.

00:57:13.210 --> 00:57:16.160
It's not a function of time.

00:57:16.160 --> 00:57:18.310
This is not always the case.

00:57:18.310 --> 00:57:20.710
For example, when I
want to solve a problem,

00:57:20.710 --> 00:57:24.190
light interacts
