00:59:31.090 --> 00:59:34.405
So let me use, you
know that constant

00:59:34.405 --> 00:59:39.650
is E. It's not an incident
I use E. Because this E,

00:59:39.650 --> 00:59:42.800
it turns out, is the energy.

00:59:42.800 --> 00:59:45.320
So this part is easy to solve.

00:59:45.320 --> 00:59:47.990
It's the first order of
differential equation.

00:59:47.990 --> 00:59:52.790
When I solve it, what I have
is y is a function of time

00:59:52.790 --> 00:59:55.700
is exponential.

01:00:00.670 --> 01:00:10.390
So say a constant times
exponential minus i, E over h,

01:00:10.390 --> 01:00:11.050
times t.

01:00:15.250 --> 01:00:18.930
So E over h, I just use
another notation omega.

01:00:18.930 --> 01:00:21.270
If you think of
this as E is energy.

01:00:21.270 --> 01:00:26.190
Let me [INAUDIBLE] So
it's minus i omega t.

01:00:26.190 --> 01:00:28.030
So that's the time dependent.

01:00:32.260 --> 01:00:35.530
And the space
dependent term, once I

01:00:35.530 --> 01:00:40.840
have the separation of variable,
the space dependent term--

01:00:40.840 --> 01:00:49.080
now is, you see here is I
multiply this E times psi.

01:00:49.080 --> 01:01:03.890
So what I have is the plus
u minus E psi equals 0.

01:01:03.890 --> 01:01:07.910
So this is a time-independent
Schrodinger equation.

01:01:11.150 --> 01:01:15.350
And this is the one
that you use when

01:01:15.350 --> 01:01:21.110
you want to solve most problems,
what's the energy of matter?

01:01:21.110 --> 01:01:22.790
What's the energy
of the electron?

01:01:22.790 --> 01:01:27.140
What's the energy
you say crystal?

01:01:27.140 --> 01:01:30.840
What are the allowable energy
of atoms vibration in crystal?

01:01:30.840 --> 01:01:34.670
This is the
Schrodinger equation--

01:01:34.670 --> 01:01:38.180
time independent
Schrodinger equation.

01:01:38.180 --> 01:01:45.610
And the difference of this
is, if you look at it,

01:01:45.610 --> 01:01:50.310
what's different for each
